When PSE controller registers during boot, PoE ports that are already
enabled can be prematurely disabled by the regulator framework's
late_initcall cleanup (~30 seconds after boot). This occurs when
dependent hardware (e.g., switch firmware update) causes network
interfaces to initialize after the regulator cleanup runs.

The regulator_init_complete() function disables all regulators with
use_count == 0 that don't have always_on constraint. PSE regulators
meet these criteria during the boot window, causing PoE devices to
lose power. We cannot set always_on also as we'd like to disable
PoE ports on a user request.

Fix this by extending defer work time to 180s. At this point all
used regulators should have their customers and use_count > 0.

Signed-off-by: Piotr Kubik <piotr.kubik@adtran.com>
---
--- a/drivers/regulator/core.c
+++ b/drivers/regulator/core.c
@@ -6607,7 +6607,7 @@ static int __init regulator_init_complet
 	 */
 	queue_delayed_work(system_freezable_wq,
 			   &regulator_init_complete_work,
-			   msecs_to_jiffies(30000));
+			   msecs_to_jiffies(180000));
 
 	return 0;
 }
